 "method": "resolvable 2-(v,3,2) design(30) on Z_5 x 6 classes (bowler = 5*class + x + 1), lane pairs as 2 tracks of 5; the automorphism x -> x+1 also rotates the lane pairs (group on lane l moves to l+1). Each round = base week(s) developed mod 5 + invariant weeks (two transversal-trio orbits on a partition of the classes, each on its own track). Base weeks by simulated annealing on pair-orbit counts (every pure/mixed difference exactly lambda times), lanes by DFS on (lane - x) residues per class, so every bowler is on every lane pair floor/ceil(r/n) times. No trio recurs. Code: 3way/tools/ext40/ (zn.c / zm.c). Week order annealed for prefix balance; positions by de Werra edge colouring. Design data: BASE 0 0: {2.2,1.0,3.0}@0 {5.4,1.3,1.1}@9 {1.4,0.0,1.2}@5 {4.4,4.0,3.2}@6 {2.0,2.4,0.2}@4 {0.4,5.2,3.3}@1 {3.1,4.2,4.1}@8 {3.4,5.1,2.3}@3 {4.3,5.0,2.1}@2 {0.1,0.3,5.3}@7 | BASE 0 1: {0.0,3.0,2.3}@6 {5.4,0.3,4.4}@1 {0.2,1.0,4.0}@7 {1.3,0.1,1.2}@4 {5.3,5.2,4.1}@5 {5.1,2.4,2.1}@0 {3.4,0.4,3.2}@8 {1.1,2.0,4.3}@9 {3.3,3.1,2.2}@2 {1.4,5.0,4.2}@3 | BASE 0 2: {5.0,5.2,2.1}@8 {4.0,3.1,5.4}@9 {1.2,0.2,3.3}@2 {0.1,2.3,3.2}@0 {3.4,1.0,3.0}@5 {0.3,0.0,0.4}@7 {1.1,5.1,5.3}@4 {1.3,4.1,4.3}@1 {2.4,4.2,4.4}@3 {1.4,2.0,2.2}@6 | BASE 0 3: {0.4,4.3,3.1}@4 {3.3,3.4,2.1}@6 {4.4,0.2,3.0}@2 {2.2,0.3,5.2}@0 {5.1,5.0,1.2}@8 {4.2,2.0,5.3}@7 {2.4,2.3,1.3}@5 {4.1,0.1,5.4}@9 {3.2,4.0,1.4}@3 {1.0,0.0,1.1}@1 | INV 0: [{1.0,3.1,4.1}@9 {0.0,2.1,5.2}@3 ] [{3.0,4.1,5.0}@0 {0.0,1.3,2.0}@8 ] [{0.0,3.2,5.1}@7 {1.0,2.0,4.4}@1 ] [{1.0,3.2,5.2}@2 {0.0,2.0,4.0}@5 ] [{1.0,2.3,4.4}@9 {0.0,3.4,5.0}@1 ] [{0.0,2.1,4.2}@4 {1.0,3.3,5.4}@5 ] [{0.0,2.4,4.3}@7 {1.0,3.2,5.0}@4 ] [{2.0,3.0,5.2}@9 {0.0,1.4,4.1}@1 ] [{1.0,2.4,3.4}@9 {0.0,4.4,5.4}@4 ] Round 2 = round 1 under a lane-pair permutation and a bowler relabelling (bipartite matching, schedlib.second_round) so lane totals are floor/ceil, keeping the try with the fewest repeated trios. Positions equitable over both rounds."
